From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 12:06:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03834/11362] [outer-loop] Fix the recurring A6
 integration-parity TAUTOLOGY false-positive (no gate weakening)

Operator-directed ("fix it"). PHASE A6 (INTEGRATION) logged FLAGGED across .429/.430/.431 on the HONEST
equality live_first_win_rate_integrated == live_first_win_rate_pre_integration (delta=0.0 because the A1/A2
levers nulled). Root cause: adversarial_verify's TAUTOLOGY carve-out (_declared_null_delta_descriptor)
ALREADY exempts this (downgrades CRITICAL->WARN), but the integration module emitted its guard as a
`tautology_guard` PROSE field under a name the linter does not read.

FIX (satisfy the existing STRICT carve-out -- NOT a gate edit): experiment_4681_integration_gate.build_artifact
now emits, when both deltas are ~0, the two fields the carve-out reads: null_delta_methodology_note (non-empty)
+ positive_control_passed (= parity_test_green AND no_regression_vs_pre_integration). The positive control GATES
the exemption: an UNVALIDATED integration (parity failed / regression) is NOT excused, so a fabricator cannot
dodge by claiming "no change". Verified: the patched fields downgrade the real .431 A6 flag critical->warn (no
quarantine); the gate stays strict for genuine fabrications.

Pinned by tests/python/test_adversarial_verify_control_treatment_null.py CTNULL-5 (markers -> WARN not
quarantined) + CTNULL-6 (no passing control -> still CRITICAL); 7 passed. known-issues directs every future
A6 task to emit the two fields (modules are agent-generated per milestone). scripts/adversarial_verify.py
UNCHANGED -- the fabrication gate is not weakened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
